include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// Windows stupidly treats 8-bit filenames as some dopey code page,
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// rather than utf-8. If we want to use utf8 filenames, we have to
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// convert them to WCHAR explicitly and call WCHAR versions of the
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// file functions. So, ok, we do.
