include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://                     Instantiated data structures
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// This is an attempt to implement a templated data structure.
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// What you do is define a struct foo, and then include several
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// pointer fields to struct foo in your struct. Then you call
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// the instantiator, which creates the functions that implement
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// the data structure. This requires massive undebuggable #defines,
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// so we limit the cases where we do this.
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// AA tree is an encoding of a 2-3 tree whereas RB trees encode a 2-3-4 tree;
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// much simpler code due to fewer cases.
