include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://                             Pointer Nulling
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://  This lets you automatically NULL dangling pointers to "registered"
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://  objects. Note that you have to make sure you call the appropriate
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://  functions when you free or realloc blocks of memory that contain
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://  pointers or pointer targets. stb.h can automatically do this for
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://  stb_arr, or for all frees/reallocs if it's wrapping them.
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:#ifdef STB_NPTR
