include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// get a list of all the files recursively underneath 'dir'
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// cache_file is used to store a copy of the directory tree to speed up
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// later calls. It must be unique to 'dir' and the current working
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// directory! Otherwise who knows what will happen (a good solution
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// is to put it _in_ dir, but this API doesn't force that).
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// Also, it might be possible to break this if you have two different processes
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// do a call to stb_dirtree_get() with the same cache file at about the same
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// time, but I _think_ it might just work.
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// i needed to build an identical data structure representing the state of
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// a mirrored copy WITHOUT bothering to rescan it (i.e. we're mirroring to
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// it WITHOUT scanning it, e.g. it's over the net), so this requires access
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// to all of the innards.
