include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://                        stb_dupe
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// stb_dupe is a duplicate-finding system for very, very large data
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// structures--large enough that sorting is too slow, but not so large
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// that we can't keep all the data in memory. using it works as follows:
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://     1. create an stb_dupe:
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://          provide a hash function
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://          provide an equality function
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://          provide an estimate for the size
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://          optionally provide a comparison function
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://     2. traverse your data, 'adding' pointers to the stb_dupe
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://     3. finish and ask for duplicates
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://        the stb_dupe will discard its intermediate data and build
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://        a collection of sorted lists of duplicates, with non-duplicate
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://        entries omitted entirely
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://  Implementation strategy:
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://     while collecting the N items, we keep a hash table of approximate
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://     size sqrt(N). (if you tell use the N up front, the hash table is
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://     just that size exactly)
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://     each entry in the hash table is just an stb__arr of pointers (no need
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://     to use stb_ps, because we don't need to delete from these)
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://     for step 3, for each entry in the hash table, we apply stb_dupe to it
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://     recursively. once the size gets small enough (or doesn't decrease
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://     significantly), we switch to either using qsort() on the comparison
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://     function, or else we just do the icky N^2 gather
