include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// This is an attempt to implement a templated sorting algorithm.
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// To use it, you have to explicitly instantiate it as a _function_,
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// then you call that function. This allows the comparison to be inlined,
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// giving the sort similar performance to C++ sorts.
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// It implements quicksort with three-way-median partitioning (generally
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// well-behaved), with a final insertion sort pass.
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// When you define the compare expression, you should assume you have
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// elements of your array pointed to by 'a' and 'b', and perform the comparison
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// on those. OR you can use one or more statements; first say '0;', then
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// write whatever code you want, and compute the result into a variable 'c'.
