include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://                         Fast malloc implementation
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://   This is a clone of TCMalloc, but without the thread support.
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://      1. large objects are allocated directly, page-aligned
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://      2. small objects are allocated in homogeonous heaps, 0 overhead
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://   We keep an allocation table for pages a la TCMalloc. This would
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://   require 4MB for the entire address space, but we only allocate
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://   the parts that are in use. The overhead from using homogenous heaps
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://   everywhere is 3MB. (That is, if you allocate 1 object of each size,
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://   you'll use 3MB.)
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:#if defined(STB_DEFINE) && ((defined(_WIN32) && !defined(_M_AMD64)) || defined(STB_FASTMALLOC))
