include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://                         Source code constants
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// This is a trivial system to let you specify constants in source code,
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// then while running you can change the constants.
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// Note that you can't wrap the #defines, because we need to know their
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// names. So we provide a pre-wrapped version without 'STB_' for convenience;
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// to request it, #define STB_CONVENIENT_H, yielding:
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://       KI -- integer
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://       KU -- unsigned integer
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://       KF -- float
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://       KD -- double
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://       KS -- string constant
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h://
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// Defaults to functioning in debug build, not in release builds.
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:// To force on, define STB_ALWAYS_H
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:#ifdef STB_CONVENIENT_H
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:#define KI(x) STB_I(x)
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:#define KU(x) STB_UI(x)
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:#define KF(x) STB_F(x)
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:#define KD(x) STB_D(x)
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:#define KS(x) STB_S(x)
include/stb-master/deprecated/stb.h:#endif
