include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_gl.h:// like gluPerspective, but:
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_gl.h://    fov is chosen to satisfy both hfov <= max_hfov & vfov <= max_vfov;
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_gl.h://            set one to 179 or 0 to ignore it
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_gl.h://    zoom is applied separately, so you can do linear zoom without
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_gl.h://            mucking with trig with fov; 1 -> use exact fov
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_gl.h://    'aspect' is inferred from the current viewport, and ignores the
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_gl.h://            possibility of non-square pixels
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_gl.h:extern void stbgl_Perspective(float zoom, float max_hfov, float max_vfov, float znear, float zfar);
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_gl.h:extern void stbgl_PerspectiveViewport(int x, int y, int w, int h, float zoom, float max_hfov, float max_vfov, float znear, float zfar);
