include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h:// stb_glprog v0.02 public domain         functions to reduce GLSL boilerplate
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h:// http://nothings.org/stb/stb_glprog.h   especially with GL1 + ARB extensions
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h:// Following defines *before* including have following effects:
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://     STB_GLPROG_IMPLEMENTATION
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://           creates the implementation
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://     STB_GLPROG_STATIC
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://           forces the implementation to be static (private to file that creates it)
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://     STB_GLPROG_ARB
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://           uses ARB extension names for GLSL functions and enumerants instead of core names
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://     STB_GLPROG_ARB_DEFINE_EXTENSIONS
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://           instantiates function pointers needed, static to implementing file
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://           to avoid collisions (but will collide if implementing file also
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://           defines any; best to isolate this to its own file in this case).
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://           This will try to automatically #include glext.h, but if it's not
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://           in the default include directories you'll need to include it
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://           yourself and define the next macro.
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://     STB_GLPROG_SUPPRESS_GLEXT_INCLUDE
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://           disables the automatic #include of glext.h which is normally
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://           forced by STB_GLPROG_ARB_DEFINE_EXTENSIONS
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h:// So, e.g., sample usage on an old Windows compiler:
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://     #define STB_GLPROG_IMPLEMENTATION
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://     #define STB_GLPROG_ARB_DEFINE_EXTENSIONS
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://     #include <windows.h>
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://     #include "gl/gl.h"
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://     #include "stb_glprog.h"
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h:// Note though that the header-file version of this (when you don't define
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h:// STB_GLPROG_IMPLEMENTATION) still uses GLint and such, so you basically
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h:// can only include it in places where you're already including GL, especially
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h:// on Windows where including "gl.h" requires (some of) "windows.h".
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h://
include/stb-master/tests/caveview/stb_glprog.h:// See following comment blocks for function documentation.
