include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h:// stb_connected_components - v0.96 - public domain connected components on grids
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://                                                 http://github.com/nothings/stb
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h:// Finds connected components on 2D grids for testing reachability between
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h:// two points, with fast updates when changing reachability (e.g. on one machine
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h:// it was typically 0.2ms w/ 1024x1024 grid). Each grid square must be "open" or
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h:// "closed" (traversable or untraversable), and grid squares are only connected
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h:// to their orthogonal neighbors, not diagonally.
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h:// In one source file, create the implementation by doing something like this:
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   #define STBCC_GRID_COUNT_X_LOG2    10
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   #define STBCC_GRID_COUNT_Y_LOG2    10
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   #define STB_CONNECTED_COMPONENTS_IMPLEMENTATION
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   #include "stb_connected_components.h"
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h:// The above creates an implementation that can run on maps up to 1024x1024.
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h:// Map sizes must be a multiple of (1<<(LOG2/2)) on each axis (e.g. 32 if LOG2=10,
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h:// 16 if LOG2=8, etc.) (You can just pad your map with untraversable space.)
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h:// MEMORY USAGE
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   Uses about 6-7 bytes per grid square (e.g. 7MB for a 1024x1024 grid).
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   Uses a single worst-case allocation which you pass in.
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h:// PERFORMANCE
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   On a core i7-2700K at 3.5 Ghz, for a particular 1024x1024 map (map_03.png):
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://       Creating map                   : 44.85 ms
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://       Making one square   traversable:  0.27 ms    (average over 29,448 calls)
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://       Making one square untraversable:  0.23 ms    (average over 30,123 calls)
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://       Reachability query:               0.00001 ms (average over 4,000,000 calls)
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   On non-degenerate maps update time is O(N^0.5), but on degenerate maps like
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   checkerboards or 50% random, update time is O(N^0.75) (~2ms on above machine).
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h:// CHANGELOG
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://
