include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h:// ALGORITHM
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   The NxN grid map is split into sqrt(N) x sqrt(N) blocks called
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://  "clusters". Each cluster independently computes a set of connected
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   components within that cluster (ignoring all connectivity out of
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   that cluster) using a union-find disjoint set forest. This produces a bunch
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   of locally connected components called "clumps". Each clump is (a) connected
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   within its cluster, (b) does not directly connect to any other clumps in the
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   cluster (though it may connect to them by paths that lead outside the cluster,
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   but those are ignored at this step), and (c) maintains an adjacency list of
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   all clumps in adjacent clusters that it _is_ connected to. Then a second
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   union-find disjoint set forest is used to compute connected clumps
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   globally, across the whole map. Reachability is then computed by
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   finding which clump each input point belongs to, and checking whether
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   those clumps are in the same "global" connected component.
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   The above data structure can be updated efficiently; on a change
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   of a single grid square on the map, only one cluster changes its
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   purely-local state, so only one cluster needs its clumps fully
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   recomputed. Clumps in adjacent clusters need their adjacency lists
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   updated: first to remove all references to the old clumps in the
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   rebuilt cluster, then to add new references to the new clumps. Both
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   of these operations can use the existing "find which clump each input
include/stb-master/stb_connected_components.h://   point belongs to" query to compute that adjacency information rapidly.
