include/stb-master/stb_dxt.h:
include/stb-master/stb_dxt.h:// configuration options for DXT encoder. set them in the project/makefile or just define
include/stb-master/stb_dxt.h:// them at the top.
include/stb-master/stb_dxt.h:
include/stb-master/stb_dxt.h:// STB_DXT_USE_ROUNDING_BIAS
include/stb-master/stb_dxt.h://     use a rounding bias during color interpolation. this is closer to what "ideal"
include/stb-master/stb_dxt.h://     interpolation would do but doesn't match the S3TC/DX10 spec. old versions (pre-1.03)
include/stb-master/stb_dxt.h://     implicitly had this turned on.
include/stb-master/stb_dxt.h://
include/stb-master/stb_dxt.h://     in case you're targeting a specific type of hardware (e.g. console programmers):
include/stb-master/stb_dxt.h://     NVidia and Intel GPUs (as of 2010) as well as DX9 ref use DXT decoders that are closer
include/stb-master/stb_dxt.h://     to STB_DXT_USE_ROUNDING_BIAS. AMD/ATI, S3 and DX10 ref are closer to rounding with no bias.
include/stb-master/stb_dxt.h://     you also see "(a*5 + b*3) / 8" on some old GPU designs.
include/stb-master/stb_dxt.h:// #define STB_DXT_USE_ROUNDING_BIAS
