include/stb-master/stb_image_resize_test/old_image_resize.h:// Easy-to-use API:
include/stb-master/stb_image_resize_test/old_image_resize.h://
include/stb-master/stb_image_resize_test/old_image_resize.h://     * "input pixels" points to an array of image data with 'num_channels' channels (e.g. RGB=3, RGBA=4)
include/stb-master/stb_image_resize_test/old_image_resize.h://     * input_w is input image width (x-axis), input_h is input image height (y-axis)
include/stb-master/stb_image_resize_test/old_image_resize.h://     * stride is the offset between successive rows of image data in memory, in bytes. you can
include/stb-master/stb_image_resize_test/old_image_resize.h://       specify 0 to mean packed continuously in memory
include/stb-master/stb_image_resize_test/old_image_resize.h://     * alpha channel is treated identically to other channels.
include/stb-master/stb_image_resize_test/old_image_resize.h://     * colorspace is linear or sRGB as specified by function name
include/stb-master/stb_image_resize_test/old_image_resize.h://     * returned result is 1 for success or 0 in case of an error.
include/stb-master/stb_image_resize_test/old_image_resize.h://       #define STBIR_ASSERT() to trigger an assert on parameter validation errors.
include/stb-master/stb_image_resize_test/old_image_resize.h://     * Memory required grows approximately linearly with input and output size, but with
include/stb-master/stb_image_resize_test/old_image_resize.h://       discontinuities at input_w == output_w and input_h == output_h.
include/stb-master/stb_image_resize_test/old_image_resize.h://     * These functions use a "default" resampling filter defined at compile time. To change the filter,
include/stb-master/stb_image_resize_test/old_image_resize.h://       you can change the compile-time defaults by #defining STBIR_DEFAULT_FILTER_UPSAMPLE
include/stb-master/stb_image_resize_test/old_image_resize.h://       and STBIR_DEFAULT_FILTER_DOWNSAMPLE, or you can use the medium-complexity API.
