include/stb-master/stb_image.h:   Do this:
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:      #define STB_IMAGE_IMPLEMENTATION
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:   before you include this file in *one* C or C++ file to create the implementation.
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:   // i.e. it should look like this:
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:   #include ...
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:   #include ...
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:   #include ...
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:   #define STB_IMAGE_IMPLEMENTATION
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:   #include "stb_image.h"
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:   You can #define STBI_ASSERT(x) before the #include to avoid using assert.h.
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:   And #define STBI_MALLOC, STBI_REALLOC, and STBI_FREE to avoid using malloc,realloc,free
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:   QUICK NOTES:
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:      Primarily of interest to game developers and other people who can
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:          avoid problematic images and only need the trivial interface
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:      JPEG baseline & progressive (12 bpc/arithmetic not supported, same as stock IJG lib)
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:      PNG 1/2/4/8/16-bit-per-channel
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:      TGA (not sure what subset, if a subset)
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:      BMP non-1bpp, non-RLE
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:      PSD (composited view only, no extra channels, 8/16 bit-per-channel)
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:      GIF (*comp always reports as 4-channel)
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:      HDR (radiance rgbE format)
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:      PIC (Softimage PIC)
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:      PNM (PPM and PGM binary only)
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:      Animated GIF still needs a proper API, but here's one way to do it:
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:          http://gist.github.com/urraka/685d9a6340b26b830d49
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:      - decode from memory or through FILE (define STBI_NO_STDIO to remove code)
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:      - decode from arbitrary I/O callbacks
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:      - SIMD acceleration on x86/x64 (SSE2) and ARM (NEON)
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:   Full documentation under "DOCUMENTATION" below.
