include/stb-master/stb_image.h:// gcc doesn't support sse2 intrinsics unless you compile with -msse2,
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:// which in turn means it gets to use SSE2 everywhere. This is unfortunate,
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:// but previous attempts to provide the SSE2 functions with runtime
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:// detection caused numerous issues. The way architecture extensions are
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:// exposed in GCC/Clang is, sadly, not really suited for one-file libs.
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:// New behavior: if compiled with -msse2, we use SSE2 without any
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:// detection; if not, we don't use it at all.
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:#define STBI_NO_SIMD
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:#endif
