include/stb-master/stb_image.h:// 32-bit MinGW wants ESP to be 16-byte aligned, but this is not in the
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:// Windows ABI and VC++ as well as Windows DLLs don't maintain that invariant.
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:// As a result, enabling SSE2 on 32-bit MinGW is dangerous when not
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:// simultaneously enabling "-mstackrealign".
include/stb-master/stb_image.h://
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:// See https://github.com/nothings/stb/issues/81 for more information.
include/stb-master/stb_image.h://
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:// So default to no SSE2 on 32-bit MinGW. If you've read this far and added
include/stb-master/stb_image.h:// -mstackrealign to your build settings, feel free to #define STBI_MINGW_ENABLE_SSE2.
