include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:STBTT_DEF int stbtt_InitFont(stbtt_fontinfo *info, const unsigned char *data, int offset);
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// Given an offset into the file that defines a font, this function builds
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// the necessary cached info for the rest of the system. You must allocate
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// the stbtt_fontinfo yourself, and stbtt_InitFont will fill it out. You don't
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// need to do anything special to free it, because the contents are pure
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// value data with no additional data structures. Returns 0 on failure.
