include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:STBTT_DEF int stbtt_GetCodepointShape(const stbtt_fontinfo *info, int unicode_codepoint, stbtt_vertex **vertices);
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:STBTT_DEF int stbtt_GetGlyphShape(const stbtt_fontinfo *info, int glyph_index, stbtt_vertex **vertices);
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// returns # of vertices and fills *vertices with the pointer to them
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h://   these are expressed in "unscaled" coordinates
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h://
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// The shape is a series of contours. Each one starts with
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// a STBTT_moveto, then consists of a series of mixed
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// STBTT_lineto and STBTT_curveto segments. A lineto
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// draws a line from previous endpoint to its x,y; a curveto
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// draws a quadratic bezier from previous endpoint to
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// its x,y, using cx,cy as the bezier control point.
