include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:STBTT_DEF unsigned char *stbtt_GetCodepointBitmap(const stbtt_fontinfo *info, float scale_x, float scale_y, int codepoint, int *width, int *height, int *xoff, int *yoff);
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// allocates a large-enough single-channel 8bpp bitmap and renders the
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// specified character/glyph at the specified scale into it, with
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// antialiasing. 0 is no coverage (transparent), 255 is fully covered (opaque).
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// *width & *height are filled out with the width & height of the bitmap,
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// which is stored left-to-right, top-to-bottom.
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h://
include/stb-master/stb_truetype.h:// xoff/yoff are the offset it pixel space from the glyph origin to the top-left of the bitmap
