include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h:// stb_hexwave - v0.5 - public domain, initial release 2021-04-01
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h:// A flexible anti-aliased (bandlimited) digital audio oscillator.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h:// This library generates waveforms of a variety of shapes made of
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h:// line segments. It does not do envelopes, LFO effects, etc.; it
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h:// merely tries to solve the problem of generating an artifact-free
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h:// morphable digital waveform with a variety of spectra, and leaves
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h:// it to the user to rescale the waveform and mix multiple voices, etc.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h:// Compiling:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   In one C/C++ file that #includes this file, do
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      #define STB_HEXWAVE_IMPLEMENTATION
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      #include "stb_hexwave.h"
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   Optionally, #define STB_HEXWAVE_STATIC before including
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   the header to cause the definitions to be private to the
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   implementation file (i.e. to be "static" instead of "extern").
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h:// Notes:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   Optionally performs memory allocation during initialization,
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   never allocates otherwise.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h:// License:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   See end of file for license information.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h:// Usage:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   Initialization:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://     hexwave_init(32,16,NULL); // read "header section" for alternatives
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   Create oscillator:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://     HexWave *osc = malloc(sizeof(*osc)); // or "new HexWave", or declare globally or on stack
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://     hexwave_create(osc, reflect_flag, peak_time, half_height, zero_wait);
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://       see "Waveform shapes" below for the meaning of these parameters
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   Generate audio:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://     hexwave_generate_samples(output, number_of_samples, osc, oscillator_freq)
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://       where:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://         output is a buffer where the library will store floating point audio samples
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://         number_of_samples is the number of audio samples to generate
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://         osc is a pointer to a Hexwave
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://         oscillator_freq is the frequency of the oscillator divided by the sample rate
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://       The output samples will continue from where the samples generated by the
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://       previous hexwave_generate_samples() on this oscillator ended.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   Change oscillator waveform:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://     hexwave_change(osc, reflect_flag, peak_time, half_height, zero_wait);
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://       can call in between calls to hexwave_generate_samples
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h:// Waveform shapes:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   All waveforms generated by hexwave are constructed from six line segments
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   characterized by 3 parameters.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   See demonstration: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hsUCrAsDN-M
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://                 reflect=0                          reflect=1
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://           0-----P---1                        0-----P---1    peak_time = P
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://                 .     1                            .     1
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://                /\_    :                           /\_    :
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://               /   \_  :                          /   \_  :
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://              /      \.H                         /      \.H  half_height = H
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://             /       | :                        /       | :
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://       _____/        |_:___               _____/        | :       _____
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://           .           :   \        |         .         | :      /
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://           .           :    \       |         .         | :     /
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://           .           :     \     _/         .         \_:    /
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://           .           :      \  _/           .           :_  /
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://           .          -1       \/             .          -1 \/
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://       0 - Z - - - - 1                    0 - Z - - - - 1   zero_wait = Z
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    Classic waveforms:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://                               peak    half    zero
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://                     reflect   time   height   wait
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Sawtooth          1       0       0       0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Square            1       0       1       0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Triangle          1       0.5     0       0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    Some waveforms can be produced in multiple ways, which is useful when morphing
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    into other waveforms, and there are a few more notable shapes:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://                               peak    half    zero
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://                     reflect   time   height   wait
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Sawtooth          1       1      any      0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Sawtooth (8va)    1       0      -1       0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Triangle          1       0.5     0       0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Square            1       0       1       0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Square            0       0       1       0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Triangle          0       0.5     0       0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Triangle          0       0      -1       0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      AlternatingSaw    0       0       0       0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      AlternatingSaw    0       1      any      0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Stairs            0       0       1       0.5
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    The "Sawtooth (8va)" waveform is identical to a sawtooth wave with 2x the
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    frequency, but when morphed with other values, it becomes an overtone of
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    the base frequency.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://  Morphing waveforms:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    Sweeping peak_time morphs the waveform while producing various spectra.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    Sweeping half_height effectively crossfades between two waveforms; useful, but less exciting.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    Sweeping zero_wait produces a similar effect no matter the reset of the waveform,
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://        a sort of high-pass/PWM effect where the wave becomes silent at zero_wait=1.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    You can trivially morph between any two waveforms from the above table
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    which only differ in one column.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    Crossfade between classic waveforms:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://                                            peak     half    zero
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://        Start         End         reflect   time    height   wait
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://        -----         ---         -------   ----    ------   ----
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://        Triangle      Square         0       0      -1..1    0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://        Saw           Square         1       0       0..1    0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://        Triangle      Saw            1       0.5     0..2    0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    The last morph uses uses half-height values larger than 1, which means it will
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    be louder and the output should be scaled down by half to compensate, or better
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    by dynamically tracking the morph: volume_scale = 1 - half_height/4
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    Non-crossfade morph between classic waveforms, most require changing
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    two parameters at the same time:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://                                           peak     half    zero
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Start         End         reflect    time    height   wait
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      -----         ---         -------    ----    ------   ----
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Square        Triangle      any      0..0.5   1..0     0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Square        Saw            1       0..1     1..any   0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Triangle      Saw            1     0.5..1     0..-1    0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    Other noteworthy morphs between simple shapes:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://                                                            peak     half    zero
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Start           Halfway       End          reflect    time    height   wait
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      -----           ---------     ---          -------    ----    ------   ----
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Saw (8va,neg)                Saw (pos)        1       0..1      -1      0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Saw (neg)                    Saw (pos)        1       0..1       0      0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Triangle                     AlternatingSaw   0       0..1      -1      0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      AlternatingSaw  Triangle     AlternatingSaw   0       0..1       0      0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Square                       AlternatingSaw   0       0..1       1      0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Triangle        Triangle     AlternatingSaw   0       0..1    -1..1     0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Square                       AlternatingSaw   0       0..1     1..0     0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Saw (8va)       Triangle     Saw              1       0..1    -1..1     0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      Saw (neg)                    Saw (pos)        1       0..1     0..1     0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://      AlternatingSaw               AlternatingSaw   0       0..1     0..any   0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   The last entry is noteworthy because the morph from the halfway point to either
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   endpoint sounds very different. For example, an LFO sweeping back and forth over
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   the whole range will morph between the middle timbre and the AlternatingSaw
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   timbre in two different ways, alternating.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   Entries with "any" for half_height are whole families of morphs, as you can pick
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   any value you want as the endpoint for half_height.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   You can always morph between any two waveforms with the same value of 'reflect'
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   by just sweeping the parameters simultaneously. There will never be artifacts
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   and the result will always be useful, if not necessarily what you want.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   You can vary the sound of two-parameter morphs by ramping them differently,
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   e.g. if the morph goes from t=0..1, then square-to-triangle looks like:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://        peak_time   = lerp(t, 0, 0.5)
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://        half_height = lerp(t, 1, 0  )
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   but you can also do things like:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://        peak_time   = lerp(smoothstep(t), 0, 0.5)
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://        half_height = cos(PI/2 * t)
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h:// How it works:
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   hexwave use BLEP to bandlimit discontinuities and BLAMP
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   to bandlimit C1 discontinuities. This is not polyBLEP
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   (polynomial BLEP), it is table-driven BLEP. It is
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   also not minBLEP (minimum-phase BLEP), as that complicates
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   things for little benefit once BLAMP is involved.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   The previous oscillator frequency is remembered, and when
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   the frequency changes, a BLAMP is generated to remove the
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   C1 discontinuity, which reduces artifacts for sweeps/LFO.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   Changes to an oscillator timbre using hexwave_change() actually
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   wait until the oscillator finishes its current cycle. All
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   waveforms with non-zero "zero_wait" settings pass through 0
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   and have 0-slope at the start of a cycle, which means changing
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   the settings is artifact free at that time. (If zero_wait is 0,
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   the code still treats it as passing through 0 with 0-slope; it'll
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   apply the necessary fixups to make it artifact free as if it does
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   transition to 0 with 0-slope vs. the waveform at the end of
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   the cycle, then adds the fixups for a non-0 and non-0 slope
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   at the start of the cycle, which cancels out if zero_wait is 0,
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   and still does the right thing if zero_wait is 0 when the
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   settings are updated.)
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   BLEP/BLAMP normally requires overlapping buffers, but this
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   is hidden from the user by generating the waveform to a
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   temporary buffer and saving the overlap regions internally
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   between calls. (It is slightly more complicated; see code.)
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   By design all shapes have 0 DC offset; this is one reason
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   hexwave uses zero_wait instead of standard PWM.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   The internals of hexwave could support any arbitrary shape
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   made of line segments, but I chose not to expose this
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   generality in favor of a simple, easy-to-use API.
