include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://         width: size of BLEP, from 4..64, larger is slower & more memory but less aliasing
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://    oversample: 2+, number of subsample positions, larger uses more memory but less noise
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://   user_buffer: optional, if provided the library will perform no allocations.
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://                16*width*(oversample+1) bytes, must stay allocated as long as library is used
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://                technically it only needs:   8*( width * (oversample  + 1))
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://                                           + 8*((width *  oversample) + 1)  bytes
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h://
include/stb-master/stb_hexwave.h:// width can be larger than 64 if you define STB_HEXWAVE_MAX_BLEP_LENGTH to a larger value
