include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// stb_voxel_render.h - v0.89 - Sean Barrett, 2015 - public domain
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// This library helps render large-scale "voxel" worlds for games,
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// in this case, one with blocks that can have textures and that
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// can also be a few shapes other than cubes.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://    Video introduction:
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://       http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2vnTtiLrV1w
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://    Minecraft-viewer sample app (not very simple though):
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://       http://github.com/nothings/stb/tree/master/tests/caveview
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// It works by creating triangle meshes. The library includes
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://    - converter from dense 3D arrays of block info to vertex mesh
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://    - vertex & fragment shaders for the vertex mesh
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://    - assistance in setting up shader state
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// For portability, none of the library code actually accesses
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// the 3D graphics API. (At the moment, it's not actually portable
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// since the shaders are GLSL only, but patches are welcome.)
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// You have to do all the caching and tracking of vertex buffers
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// yourself. However, you could also try making a game with
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// a small enough world that it's fully loaded rather than
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// streaming. Currently the preferred vertex format is 20 bytes
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// per quad. There are designs to allow much more compact formats
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// with a slight reduction in shader features, but no roadmap
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// for actually implementing them.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// USAGE
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   #define the symbol STB_VOXEL_RENDER_IMPLEMENTATION in *one*
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   C/C++ file before the #include of this file; the implementation
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   will be generated in that file.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   If you define the symbols STB_VOXEL_RENDER_STATIC, then the
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   implementation will be private to that file.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// FEATURES
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - you can choose textured blocks with the features below,
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     or colored voxels with 2^24 colors and no textures.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - voxels are mostly just cubes, but there's support for
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     half-height cubes and diagonal slopes, half-height
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     diagonals, and even odder shapes especially for doing
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     more-continuous "ground".
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - texture coordinates are projections along one of the major
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     axes, with the per-texture scaling.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - a number of aspects of the shader and the vertex format
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     are configurable; the library generally takes care of
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     coordinating the vertex format with the mesh for you.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// FEATURES (SHADER PERSPECTIVE)
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - vertices aligned on integer lattice, z on multiples of 0.5
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - per-vertex "lighting" or "ambient occlusion" value (6 bits)
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - per-vertex texture crossfade (3 bits)
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - per-face texture #1 id (8-bit index into array texture)
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - per-face texture #2 id (8-bit index into second array texture)
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - per-face color (6-bit palette index, 2 bits of per-texture boolean enable)
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - per-face 5-bit normal for lighting calculations & texture coord computation
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - per-face 2-bit texture matrix rotation to rotate faces
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - indexed-by-texture-id scale factor (separate for texture #1 and texture #2)
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - indexed-by-texture-#2-id blend mode (alpha composite or modulate/multiply);
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     the first is good for decals, the second for detail textures, "light maps",
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     etc; both modes are controlled by texture #2's alpha, scaled by the
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     per-vertex texture crossfade and the per-face color (if enabled on texture #2);
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     modulate/multiply multiplies by an extra factor of 2.0 so that if you
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     make detail maps whose average brightness is 0.5 everything works nicely.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - ambient lighting: half-lambert directional plus constant, all scaled by vertex ao
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - face can be fullbright (emissive), controlled by per-face color
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - installable lighting, with default single-point-light
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   - installable fog, with default hacked smoothstep
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://  Note that all the variations of lighting selection and texture
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://  blending are run-time conditions in the shader, so they can be
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://  intermixed in a single mesh.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// INTEGRATION ARC
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   The way to get this library to work from scratch is to do the following:
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://      Step 1. define STBVOX_CONFIG_MODE to 0
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://        This mode uses only vertex attributes and uniforms, and is easiest
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://        to get working. It requires 32 bytes per quad and limits the
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://        size of some tables to avoid hitting uniform limits.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://      Step 2. define STBVOX_CONFIG_MODE to 1
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://        This requires using a texture buffer to store the quad data,
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://        reducing the size to 20 bytes per quad.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://      Step 3: define STBVOX_CONFIG_PREFER_TEXBUFFER
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://        This causes some uniforms to be stored as texture buffers
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://        instead. This increases the size of some of those tables,
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://        and avoids a potential slow path (gathering non-uniform
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://        data from uniforms) on some hardware.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   In the future I might add additional modes that have significantly
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   smaller meshes but reduce features, down as small as 6 bytes per quad.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   See elsewhere in this file for a table of candidate modes. Switching
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   to a mode will require changing some of your mesh creation code, but
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   everything else should be seamless. (And I'd like to change the API
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   so that mesh creation is data-driven the way the uniforms are, and
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   then you wouldn't even have to change anything but the mode number.)
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// IMPROVEMENTS FOR SHIP-WORTHY PROGRAMS USING THIS LIBRARY
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   I currently tolerate a certain level of "bugginess" in this library.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   I'm referring to things which look a little wrong (as long as they
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   don't cause holes or cracks in the output meshes), or things which
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   do not produce as optimal a mesh as possible. Notable examples:
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://        -  incorrect lighting on slopes
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://        -  inefficient meshes for vheight blocks
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   I am willing to do the work to improve these things if someone is
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   going to ship a substantial program that would be improved by them.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   (It need not be commercial, nor need it be a game.) I just didn't
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   want to do the work up front if it might never be leveraged. So just
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   submit a bug report as usual (github is preferred), but add a note
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   that this is for a thing that is really going to ship. (That means
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   you need to be far enough into the project that it's clear you're
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   committed to it; not during early exploratory development.)
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// VOXEL MESH API
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   Context
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     To understand the API, make sure you first understand the feature set
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     listed above.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     Because the vertices are compact, they have very limited spatial
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     precision. Thus a single mesh can only contain the data for a limited
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     area. To make very large voxel maps, you'll need to build multiple
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     vertex buffers. (But you want this anyway for frustum culling.)
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     Each generated mesh has three components:
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://             - vertex data (vertex buffer)
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://             - face data (optional, stored in texture buffer)
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://             - mesh transform (uniforms)
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     Once you've generated the mesh with this library, it's up to you
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     to upload it to the GPU, to keep track of the state, and to render
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     it.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   Concept
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     The basic design is that you pass in one or more 3D arrays; each array
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     is (typically) one-byte-per-voxel and contains information about one
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     or more properties of some particular voxel property.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     Because there is so much per-vertex and per-face data possible
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     in the output, and each voxel can have 6 faces and 8 vertices, it
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     would require an very large data structure to describe all
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     of the possibilities, and this would cause the mesh-creation
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     process to be slow. Instead, the API provides multiple ways
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     to express each property, some more compact, others less so;
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     each such way has some limitations on what it can express.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     Note that there are so many paths and combinations, not all of them
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     have been tested. Just report bugs and I'll fix 'em.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://   Details
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://     See the API documentation in the header-file section.
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
