include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h://
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// With TexBuffer for the fixed vertex data, we can actually do
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// minecrafty non-blocks like stairs -- we still probably only
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// want 256 or so, so we can't do the equivalent of all the vheight
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// combos, but that's ok. The 256 includes baked rotations, but only
include/stb-master/stb_voxel_render.h:// some of them need it, and lots of block types share some faces.
